[Scott.Bigham@bbs.oit.unc.edu (Scott Bigham) writes:]
[] No, no, I don't want to change me, I want to change the _altar_ -- say, 
[] from an altar to Anhur to an altar to Thoth.  Changing alignment is bound
[] to annoy my deity (and besides, lawful characters could use this to make 
[] holy water at any altar they found).

there are only two types of conversions at altars:
1) you convert to the alignment of the (god of the) altar, or
2) the altar converts to your alignment.

these facts together with facts posted here recently can enable you
to arbitrary change any altar to any alignment and also allow you
to change to any alignment, with one exception, i think: chaotic
a/o lawful types cannot arbitrarily become neutral without the
aid of a neutral altar (ahem, gloves of alignment would fit nicely
here ...).

btw, there are only 4 or so interesting things you can do at an
altar (kick, drop, pray and sacrifice/offer, etc.) and you can
intuitively eliminate all but two of the options, in order to do
what you want.  then from the remaining two options you can deduce
the correct option.  see, you knew the answer all along ...

